  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "The recovery module's retry field is a static 0, so transient (retryable) tool errors are never retried, causing tool_recovery and composition failures where a single transient timeout yields UNKNOWN. Making retry a general expression that triggers a retry only when the last error is retryable and not permanent (and attempts remain) will recover transient failures without retrying permanent errors, while keeping max_attempts at 3 to bound total attempts.",
    "changes": {
      "retry": {
        "op": "and",
        "args": [
          {
            "var": "error_retryable"
          },
          {
            "op": "not",
            "args": [
              {
                "var": "error_permanent"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "max_attempts": 3
    },
    "predicted_behavior": "On transient_error events (retryable=1, permanent=0) the agent retries the same read-only tool, succeeding on attempt 2-3 and producing the correct token/answer with proper evidence. On permanent_error events (retryable=0) no retry occurs, avoiding wasted attempts. tool_recovery and composition families should flip from UNKNOWN to correct answers; memory_temporal/memory_scope failures (which are ranking, not retry, issues) remain unaffected.",
    "regression_risk": "Low-moderate: if a tool reports retryable=1 but never succeeds, up to max_attempts=3 attempts are consumed, slightly increasing latency/attempt counts; the attempts check could fail if the harness expects exactly 1 attempt on cases that are actually transient. No authority or policy changes are made."
  },
